# Reading brainstorm — 2026-11-06
#
# Ideas for syntax, file structure, tooling, artifacts and philosophy, from reading a
# mounted consumer's November work beside this repo and probing seed at dbd138dd.
# Each idea names its evidence and the plan that takes it, or says it is held.

#>journal_2026_11_06_reading_brainstorm
#:cache #!observation
#:layer #!pragmatics

^["entry"]{
 date: "2026-11-06"
 kind: #observation
 base: "main@dbd138dd; consumer tree read at its 2026-11-06 head; counts exclude archives and the consumer's mount"
}

^["thread"]{
 # The one finding the ideas share.
 claim: "Seed misreads more of what people write than it reports. Four readings are silent: a line-final <…> takes the next line's head, key = value is three loose expressions, key = @handle is a bias edge anchored at the handle, and <…> straight after a word becomes a relation. None raises an error, so neither the workbench nor its consumer saw them until a census looked."
 measured: #[
  "line-crossing medial capsules: 10 in 7 workbench files, 347 in 133 consumer files",
  "key = value lines: 2,174 in the workbench, 25,429 in the consumer, against 48,470 and 16,848 key: value lines",
  "operator-led <…> that wraps instead of filling its slot: 0 in the workbench, 28 in the consumer",
  "key = @handle or key = ~\"path\" read as bias edges: 27 in the workbench, 2,590 in the consumer; tight =@ and =~: 160 and 0",
 ]
}

^["syntax"]{
 s1_spaced_equals: "A spaced = in key position binds, as : does; a tight =x stays bias. Seed reads a = 1 as three expressions (Identifier, a bare = Operation, Literal), so 25,429 consumer lines and every .{ rank = 1 } row in this repo's plans carry no key to any reader. editing.ts already reads .{ k = v } facts by regex. | home: syntax-hardware-alignment p12, gated by reading-drift"
 s2_line_locality: "Outside an open container, no arm of a construct crosses a newline. The postfix loop already obeys this; the medial loop does not. | home: brace-slot-reading medial_stays_on_line, and philosophy p1"
 s3_angle_readings: "<…> has at least five readings: a slot (word[mode]{body}<concept>), a relation (bagel<scent>coffee), a path tag (~<tag>\"path\"), a stream list (?<a, b>), and a type parameter authors borrow from code (loader<{(), getLastError}>). Seed tells them apart by position alone. | home: brace-slot-reading ?[capsule_before_pair]"
 s4_pipe_meaning: "| is already a connector inside a term run (a | b is one expression whose connector is |) and a block-scalar opener at line end. The consumer's later mark could be a meaning for the connector it already is, alternative, read the same in {a|b} and $%[a | b], with no new lexing. | home: syntax-hardware-alignment p13"
 s5_lifecycle_in_mode: "A wonder's lifecycle could ride its mode slot: ?name[probed]{…}, so a reader sees the stage without a harvest. The consumer proposed the printed form for its contour. | home: inquiry-loop ?[lifecycle_spelling]"
 s6_typed_hole: "<&> as a hole that asks for a slot of a kind, beside * (any slot) and _ (seed's hole). Waits on query field filters. | home: lukewarm-backlog"
 s7_answer_set: "A $% list beside ~#expect or ~#answer is an answer set, not a measure. | home: vscode-authoring-probe-loop answer_set_mark (already planned)"
}

^["file_structure"]{
 f1_one_intake: "Consumer asks are taken in by four tables in four shapes (first-plugin, inquiry-loop, the vscode-lsp-roadmap PLAN table, and ground-edge-reading); one misroute (motions to a rescoped plan) went unseen for ten days. One intake file and one replies file, neither naming the consumer. | home: ask-exchange"
 f2_unread_frames: "Six optional wip frames (concept_index, recursive_improvement, parallel_work, supporting_documents, interaction_depth, risk_model) fill 2,213 of 13,170 plan lines, appear in 27 to 64 plans each, and have no reader in scripts or packages. | home: plan-tooling-design ?[unread_frames]"
 f3_consumer_corpus_by_path: "Grammar fixtures today are synthetic strings; the largest real corpus is a mounted consumer's. Read it by an explicit path at check time and keep only counts and line fingerprints here, so no consumer text is copied in. | home: reading-drift"
}

^["tooling"]{
 t1_reading_drift: "A snapshot of what each line reads as (kind, slots, arms, line span), and a check that lists lines whose reading changed. The consumer already verifies its own reader this way (986 expressions identical to the snapshot taken before a change). | home: reading-drift"
 t2_query_fields: "spw query selects capsules but --where placement=medial filters nothing, so today's three censuses were one-off scripts. Field filters on AST nodes and a count-by would make each one command. | home: cli-sense-reorientation query_where_fields"
 t3_asks_check: "A verb that reads a consumer's ask files by path and reports asks with no home, homes that are archived or rescoped, and status that disagrees with the home plan. It would have caught the motions misroute. | home: ask-exchange (takes onboarding-quest collect_asks)"
}

^["artifacts"]{
 a1_release_readings: "Each parser release carries the readings of a fixed specimen set, so two releases compare by diffing two files; spw.quest's two-release specimen view waits on exactly this. | home: parser-releases release_readings"
 a2_grammar_receipt: "A grammar commit's *[verify] cites its drift: lines whose reading changed, per corpus. | home: reading-drift grammar_receipt"
 a3_replies: "What the workbench would tell a consumer (misroutes, stale claims, facts that did not reproduce) as a file the consumer reads on a pin bump. | home: ask-exchange (starts from inquiry-loop ^replies)"
}

^["philosophy"]{
 p1_reading_is_local: "What a line means is decidable from the line and the containers open around it. The note goal (a line stays a note) needs it: a reader without the tool cannot see a relation that reaches into the next line."
 p2_no_silent_readings: "A line parses into what its author wrote, or says why it does not. A misread with no diagnostic costs more than an error: an error is fixed the day it appears, a silent reading is copied for months. The four readings in ^thread all failed this."
 p3_usage_is_evidence: "Grammar decisions are weighed against what mounted corpora write, measured, not against this repo's idiom alone; the consumer writes key = value twelve times as often as this repo does."
 p4_every_field_has_a_reader: "The reader-health rule the consumer asks of plugins (a field nobody reads fails the run) holds for plan frames, emit fields and stamps alike."
 p5_character_is_meaning: "One table of characters; each workspace's names for them are aliases over it (the consumer's mark_goal). Settles cross-surface naming by layering, not by a winner."
 home: "plan-ecology-clustering doctrine_reading, which proposes p1 to p4 for the canon after the owner reads them; p5 is relationship-contours ?[cross_surface_copy]"
}
